      "mergeID": "6a26d1e80ee3cda96eddbd73",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When opening the menu in VRChat on Android, image elements such as world thumbnails, user avatars, bundles, and items appear discolored with a yellow-green or yellowish tint. Additionally, the images are fragmented into square blocks or rectangular pieces, resulting in blocky noise or mosaic-like rendering artifacts. \n\nText and UI frames, however, are displayed correctly.\n\nAs I have confirmed that other users are experiencing the same issue, it is likely not limited to a specific device or environment.\n\n[Occurrence Details]\n\n- Date/Time: Starting from 2026/06/05\n\n- Device: Galaxy S25 Ultra (Android)\n\n- VRChat Version: S:Release_1626 V:2026.2.2\n\n- Location: Any menu or screen where images are present\n\n- Frequency: Every time (Consistent)\n\n- After Restart: Issue persists\n\n[Reproduction Steps]\n\n1. Launch VRChat.\n\n2. Open the menu.\n\n3. View the Friends list, World list, or Notifications.\n\n4. Observe that thumbnails and other images are corrupted with a yellow-green tint.\n\n[Expected Behavior]\n\nThumbnails and other images should be displayed correctly with their original colors and clarity.\n\n[Actual Behavior]\n\nImages turn yellow-green and become unrecognizable due to severe rendering corruption.\n\nI have attached screenshots for reference. Please investigate this matter.\n\n---\n\nNote:\n\nIn the attached images, personal information has been pixelated. \n\nThe UI itself is working correctly and has no issues.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Thumbnails and images are corrupted with a yellow-green tint",
